title: Card games
intro: Decks, hands and play zones, with no code: shuffle and deal, draw, and play cards by dragging them onto the table, by the rules each place on it sets.
project: Empty | Card Table

chapter: A deck, a hand and a table | Entity > Genres > Cards > Deck
create: Deck
expectcount: Hand = 1
expectcount: Play Zone = 1
expectcount: Discard Pile = 1
explain: component:Deck | Deck | A deck is a pile of cards: the cards inside it, twenty here, Sun and Moon from one to ten. It's shuffled as the game starts, with the game's own random numbers.
explain: field:Deck.Table | From a table | Or it makes its cards from a table of game data, a card for each row, with the row's title, text, value and color.
select: Hand
explain: component:Hand | Hand | The deck brought along a hand that draws five cards as the game starts and fans them out, a play zone to play them onto, and a discard pile.
select: Play Zone
set: PlayZone.Limit = 1
explain: field:PlayZone.Accepts | Rules | A play zone has rules: the kinds of card it takes, which hands may play onto it, and a limit. This one holds one card.
deselect
create: Text
rename: Hand Count
set: Transform.Position.Y = 4
set: Text.Size = 0.5
add: Counter
set: Counter.Track = Hand
set: Counter.Output = Count
set: Counter.Format = In hand: {0}
explain: field:Counter.Output | Outputs | Decks, hands and zones say how many cards they hold, for a counter, a bar or a text to show. This counter shows the cards in the hand.

chapter: Playing | Drag a card onto the table
play
wait: 1.5
expectvalue: Hand Count.Counter.Value = 5
explain: game | Dealt | Shuffled, and dealt a card at a time into a fan.
gameclick: Deck
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Hand Count.Counter.Value = 6
say: Clicking the deck draws another card.
gamedrag: Hand > Play Zone
wait: 0.8
expectvalue: Play Zone.PlayZone.Played = 1
expectvalue: Hand Count.Counter.Value = 5
explain: game | Played | Drag a card onto the zone, and it's played and slides into place.
gamedrag: Hand > Play Zone
wait: 0.8
expectvalue: Play Zone.PlayZone.Played = 1
expectvalue: Hand Count.Counter.Value = 5
say: The zone holds one card, so the next slides back to the hand.
gamedrag: Hand > Discard Pile
wait: 0.8
expectvalue: Hand Count.Counter.Value = 4
say: The discard pile takes cards dragged onto it.
tap: Right
tap: Space
wait: 0.3
tap: Space
wait: 0.8
expectvalue: Hand Count.Counter.Value = 3
say: With the keys or a gamepad, left and right pick a card, and Space takes it up and plays it where it can go.
stop
say: That's decks, hands and play zones, with no code. Decks shuffle, draw and refill from their discard pile, hands play on their side's turn, and in a network game nobody's machine is sent the deck's order or another player's hidden hand.
